'''The Virtual Reality Show''', usually shortened to '''TVRS''', is the YouTube channel of '''PHIA''' (also known online as '''PHIAbunny'''). She started it in February 2020 to talk about VR from inside VR, and it now has avatar tutorials, VR hardware videos and guides for people new to VRChat. She introduces herself on the channel as the show's virtual host.<ref name="otakify" /><ref name="yt-about">[https://www.youtube.com/@TheVirtualRealityShow/about "The Virtual Reality Show"] on ''YouTube''. Shows the channel's join date (February 17, 2020), subscriber count, video count and description. Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref> As of November 10, 2026, the channel had about 279,000 subscribers and 127 videos.<ref name="yt-about" />

The show lives in VRChat too, with a [[Special:MyLanguage/Groups|group]] and a world called '''TVRS Studio''' where monthly live events are held.<ref name="steam-2024" /><ref name="vrclist" /> Four of its videos are linked from this wiki's [[Special:MyLanguage/Getting Started|Getting Started]] page.

[[File:TVRS_Live_Events_Banner.webp|thumb|Image for The Virtual Reality Show's live events, from VRChat's March 2024 announcement on Steam.<ref name="steam-2024" />]]

== History ==

=== Before the show ===
PHIA had little interest in VR until the second half of 2019, when she got hooked on Chloma, a Japanese fashion brand that had teamed up with the free character creator VRoid Studio to sell virtual versions of its clothes. She wanted to wear them, so she made a character of her own, her PHIA model. She had never played VRChat, but she wanted somewhere to use the model, and she joined. Before long, she said, her whole life revolved around VR.<ref name="otakify">[https://otakify.com/anime-blog/virtual-reality-show-with-phiabunny "Virtual Reality Show! with PHIABUNNY"] on ''Otakify''. March 2020 (interview with PHIA). Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref>

=== A show made in a day ===
The idea came on a drive to university in early 2020. PHIA was listening to an interview with DigitrevX, one of the minds behind Projekt Melody, and realized she cared far more about this than about what she was studying. She went home that day, wrote a script, filmed and edited a video, and made a YouTube channel.<ref name="otakify" />

YouTube lists the channel's creation date as February 17, 2020, and the first video, ''Projekt Melody (Virtual CamGirl?!)'', went up the same day.<ref name="yt-first">[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ziSqWnvKTO8 "Projekt Melody (Virtual CamGirl?!)"] on ''YouTube'' (The Virtual Reality Show). Dated February 17, 2020. Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref>

=== Meeting Porter Robinson ===
The show's first months also include a meeting with Porter Robinson. PHIA had made a VR model of the musician Porter Robinson about four months before her interview, after a friend and she talked about recreating ''Second Sky'' in VR. She posted a picture of it on the Porter Robinson subreddit, joking that he should get in touch about the download, and forgot about it. Two days later he messaged her: he couldn't get the model into VRChat. Within half an hour they were in VRChat together, swapping the model, and they kept talking and wandered through worlds for a while afterward.<ref name="otakify" />

On March 20, 2020, the channel uploaded ''Thank you, Porter Robinson.''<ref name="yt-porter">[https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6-sKFABRnos "Thank you, Porter Robinson."] on ''YouTube'' (The Virtual Reality Show). Dated March 20, 2020. Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref> PHIA said the show's audience grew after he took an interest in it.<ref name="otakify" />

=== The first year ===
Through 2020 the channel posted a lot of how-tos: using VirtualCast, building a virtual YouTuber model in VRoid Studio, bringing a VRoid avatar into VRChat. There were headset comparisons and trips through VRChat worlds like Virtual Market 4. Two videos that year thanked viewers for reaching 5,000 and then 10,000 subscribers.<ref name="yt-videos">[https://www.youtube.com/@TheVirtualRealityShow/videos "Videos"] on ''YouTube'' (The Virtual Reality Show). Upload dates and view counts are taken from each video's own YouTube page. Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref> The tutorials ''How to be a Virtual Youtuber! Complete Guide'' and ''Make a custom Vtubing model with VRoid Studio for FREE!'' have each passed a million views.<ref name="yt-videos" />

=== Going full time ===
By August 2021, a ''CG Garage'' podcast page said, the show had passed 100,000 YouTube and Twitch subscribers in a little over a year, and running it had become PHIA's full-time job. The podcast introduced her as its first virtual guest.<ref name="cg-garage">[https://www.chaos.com/cg-garage/sophia-phia-bollinger-the-virtual-reality-show ''CG Garage'' podcast episode with PHIA] by Christopher Nichols on ''Chaos''. Dated August 2, 2021. Retrieved November 10, 2026.</ref>

=== A VRChat focus ===
From late 2021, a lot of the uploads are about VRChat itself. A beginners' guide came out in September 2021 and was redone in April 2024. Other videos include ''The 15 Types of VRChat Players'' (October 2022) and a how-to on uploading avatars (September 2023). A roundup of worlds to visit, featuring Thrillseeker, came out in July 2022, again in July 2023 and again in March 2025.<ref name="yt-videos" />

Hardware and other platforms still get airtime. Full-body tracking had videos in January 2022 and November 2023, a 2024 guide covered VR setups, and a May 2024 video looked at Resonite. The latest upload on the channel's page is ''The VR Cybersickness Epidemic'', from October 3, 2025.<ref name="yt-videos" />

